1. **Normalization**:
   - Normalize both strings to a consistent format, which can involve stripping out unnecessary whitespace, converting to a common case (lowercase or uppercase), and removing any line breaks or other type of whitespace that might cause issues.

   ```php
   function normalizeString($input) {
       // Convert to lowercase to ignore case sensitivity
       $input = strtolower($input);
       // Replace all spaces with hyphens (or whatever format you choose)
       $input = str_replace(' ', '-', $input);
       // Remove any trailing punctuation
